[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2424115180","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98309#issuecomment-2424115180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98309","id":2424115180,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QfQ_s","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-19T18:12:57Z","updated_at":"2024-10-19T18:12:57Z","body":"This is probably because `Godot.Collections.Array<T>` does not set the underlying array type, so the editor stores an untyped array, and when you add an element to it, it adds a default Variant which is null.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2424115180/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2424145238","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98309#issuecomment-2424145238","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98309","id":2424145238,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6QfYVW","user":{"login":"cjohnson57","id":30701749,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzAxNzQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30701749?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjohnson57","html_url":"https://github.com/cjohnson57","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjohnson57/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjohnson57/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjohnson57/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjohnson57/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjohnson57/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjohnson57/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjohnson57/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjohnson57/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjohnson57/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-19T19:01:38Z","updated_at":"2024-10-19T19:01:38Z","body":"> This is probably because `Godot.Collections.Array<T>` does not set the underlying array type, so the editor stores an untyped array, and when you add an element to it, it adds a default Variant which is null.\r\n\r\nThat's interesting, thanks for the insight!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2424145238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2442948471","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98309#issuecomment-2442948471","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98309","id":2442948471,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RnG93","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-29T00:54:32Z","updated_at":"2024-10-29T00:54:32Z","body":"> This is probably because `Godot.Collections.Array<T>` does not set the underlying array type, so the editor stores an untyped array, and when you add an element to it, it adds a default Variant which is null.\r\n\r\n@raulsntos would it be reasonable to add an alternative `godotsharp_array_new` which accepts type information, so that when some `Array<T>` is created from the c# side the native value can have `set_typed` called as appropriate? Or potentially some new `godotsharp_array_set_typed` for the `Array<T>` constructor to invoke? I probably would bias towards the former to reduce native calls but the latter feels a bit cleaner.\r\n\r\nI guess it's a bit weird in either case because in every scenario besides changing c# arrays from the editor it's c# handling type validation anyways.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2442948471/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2443327167","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98309#issuecomment-2443327167","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98309","id":2443327167,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Roja_","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-29T06:34:24Z","updated_at":"2024-10-29T06:34:24Z","body":"We likely want to match what `godot-cpp` is doing and call `Array::set_typed` in the constructor[^1]. There's already a PR that I think does this but I haven't had a chance to review it yet:\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98545\r\n\r\n[^1]: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp/blob/a98d41f62bdb8b7aa903e8e37c1faa48fe8fdae8/include/godot_cpp/variant/typed_array.hpp#L58","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2443327167/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]